      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5f2e0a4e8464150716ffd322|full_name} I am not saying that locking gestures in place should not be a function, but rather that if GestureDirect inputs are triggered, only if gestures are on should they ever trigger, them staying on past that point is a choice, but having these get stuck *just if* I have them is not ideal.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
